# Lesson 3 — GPIO Driver Progress

## Goal

Control STM32 onboard LED using direct register access.

Target:

```

GPIOC Pin 13

```

---

# Completed GPIO Concepts

## 1. Memory Mapped Registers

Learned that STM32 peripherals are accessed using fixed memory addresses.

Example:

```

RCC Base Address

0x40021000

GPIOC Base Address

0x40011000

```

Created C++ register maps.

---

# 2. RCC Register Definition

Created:

```

include/stm32f103.hpp

````

Current RCC structure:

```cpp
struct RCC
{
    volatile uint32_t CR;
    volatile uint32_t CFGR;
    volatile uint32_t CIR;
    volatile uint32_t APB2RSTR;
    volatile uint32_t APB1RSTR;
    volatile uint32_t AHBENR;
    volatile uint32_t APB2ENR;
};
````

Purpose:

Control clocks and peripheral enable.

---

# 3. GPIO Register Definition

GPIO structure:

```cpp
struct GPIO
{
    volatile uint32_t CRL;
    volatile uint32_t CRH;
    volatile uint32_t IDR;
    volatile uint32_t ODR;
    volatile uint32_t BSRR;
    volatile uint32_t BRR;
};
```

Understanding:

```
CRL  -> Configure pins 0-7

CRH  -> Configure pins 8-15

IDR  -> Read input

ODR  -> Output state

BSRR -> Atomic set/reset

BRR  -> Reset output
```

---

# 4. Enable GPIOC Clock

Completed.

GPIOC clock is controlled by:

```
RCC->APB2ENR
```

GPIOC is bit 4.

Code:

```cpp
RCC_REG->APB2ENR =
    RCC_REG->APB2ENR | (1 << 4);
```

Meaning:

```
Set APB2ENR bit 4

GPIOC clock ON
```

---

# 5. Configure PC13 Output

Completed.

PC13:

```
Port C
Pin 13
```

Since PC13 belongs to:

```
PC8 - PC15
```

configuration uses:

```
GPIOC->CRH
```

PC13 configuration location:

```
(pin - 8) × 4

(13 - 8) × 4

= 20
```

Therefore:

```
PC13 uses bits 20-23
```

---

Configuration:

```
CNF = 00
MODE = 10
```

Meaning:

```
General purpose output
Push-pull
2MHz speed
```

Code:

```cpp
GPIOC->CRH =
    GPIOC->CRH & ~(0xF << 20);


GPIOC->CRH =
    GPIOC->CRH | (0x2 << 20);
```

---

# 6. Output Control Understanding

Completed understanding of:

## ODR

Output Data Register.

Controls pin output state.

PC13:

```
ODR bit 13
```

---

## BSRR

Bit Set Reset Register.

Structure:

```
31                 16 15                 0
+--------------------+--------------------+
| Reset bits         | Set bits            |
+--------------------+--------------------+
```

Set HIGH:

```cpp
GPIOC->BSRR = (1 << 13);
```

Result:

```
PC13 = HIGH
```

---

## BRR

Bit Reset Register.

Set LOW:

```cpp
GPIOC->BRR = (1 << 13);
```

Result:

```
PC13 = LOW
```

---

# 7. LED Behaviour

STM32 Blue Pill onboard LED:

```
Active LOW
```

Therefore:

LED ON:

```cpp
GPIOC->BRR = (1 << 13);
```

LED OFF:

```cpp
GPIOC->BSRR = (1 << 13);
```

